   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Fire On The Mountain** (1 review): Reviewer wonders whether the band teased Chloe Dancer during the Fire jam [8]\n- **Dark Star** (1 review): Reviewer calls the second-set run from Dark Star through Althea, Playing in the Band, Drums, Space, The Other One and Standing on the Moon essential [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Werewolves of London**: rare: 13 archived performances [9]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **DeadCo2019-01-20.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 211 min; rated 5/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer describes the recording as clean and good [4]\n- **deadandcompany2019-01-20.neumann_skm140.sunboy.flac16**: source not stated; 21 songs; 214 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [2]. Said about its sound: Of three recordings posted at the time, this reviewer finds this Neumann one sounds best on their stereo [5]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- One of three sold-out nights; the reviewer notes a full moon eclipse coincided with this night [3]\n- Taper stood in the sand, front of board, directly in front of center, about 20-25 yards from the stage lip [2]\n- Lineup: Mickey Hart, Bill Kreutzmann, Bob Weir, John Mayer, Oteil Burbridge and Jeff Chimenti [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **DeadCo2019-01-20.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64v's>VMS5u>SD744t [1]\n- **deadandcompany2019-01-20.neumann_skm140.sunboy.flac16**: taped by Steven Weld; transferred by Steven Weld; source: Neumann SKM140(AK40's/LC3's/KM100's)>GAKables xlr>Lunatec V2>GAKables xlr>Apogee Mini-Me@24/48>AES/EBU>Sound Devices 722 @24bit/48kHz [2]",
